    "STEPS pilot. The unit calls the client's ShapePoolAlloc 1-4 times in a row on one pool that lives in the state region, and the state channel compares the whole region after every call.",
    "Why it exists: the client writes the next free index into the popped entry's own link at entry+0xA0, so the second pop reads what the first pop wrote. fn/ShapePoolAlloc (one pop, a freshly built pool) cannot see that.",
